@how own mechanism: provide a deterministic, storage-oriented substrate that maintains a coherent graph of facts across sessions (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L7 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: 
  provide a deterministic, storage-oriented substrate that maintains a coherent graph of facts across sessions

  + context: futon1’s devmap defines the substrate as deterministic and storage-first, not a session cache.

  + IF:
    storage is required to outlive sessions and remain consistent across restarts

  + HOWEVER:
    without a deterministic substrate, the graph drifts across runs and environments

  + THEN:
    treat persistence + determinism as the defining product, not a secondary feature

  + BECAUSE:
    the futon1 series exists to make the same world state appear reliably across sessions

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Define determinism tests that compare world state across restart cycles.]
    next[Document the minimal substrate contract that other futons depend on.]
